  "grid3d_force_directed": {
   "dna_declined": {
    "date": "2026-08-05",
    "axis_considered": "graph = random | tree | ring | clique | lattice (the topology the same force law is asked to lay out). NOT a `dna` block on purpose: artifact_dna_research.py reads bool(entry['dna']) as 'declared', so an empty one would enter the ledger as a promotion.",
    "reason": "The axis is real in world space and unphotographable by this bench, measured rather than guessed. cartridge_force_directed.gd's force law has NO bounding term - repulsion 0.8/d^2 against attraction 0.02*(d-0.6) - so the equilibrium SIZE is set by the edge count, which is exactly what the axis turns. Re-implementing the exact step() in Python over three seeds: clique settles at extent ~2.6 world units, random ~7-11, lattice ~11-14, ring ~16-19, tree ~15-21, and any disconnected graph (a bipartite pair) never settles at all - its components separate without bound, 23 units at 66 steps, 46 by 500, so its 'layout' is purely a function of how long you waited. capture_config_sweep places ONE camera on the union of every variant's AABB, so the dense values photograph as dots inside the sparse ones' frame.",
    "measurement": "Rasterising the relaxed layouts at the harness's real numbers (RES 760, FOV 34, PAD 1.9, node sphere r=0.06, edge cylinder r=0.012, union camera): the frame spans 91-114 world units, a node renders 0.8-1.0 PIXELS across and an edge 0.2 px. Subject share is 0.07%-0.22% of frame against the ~6% floor below which the brief says the number is about the bench; pairwise frame difference is 0.14%-0.35% against the 3% bite threshold. A sweep would run green and report INERT, and the verdict would be a fact about the framing.",
    "underlying_finding": "The shipped artifact overruns its own declared bounds by an order of magnitude. grid3d_substrate.gd declares bounds = Vector3(2.0, 1.5, 2.0) and initialize() seeds inside it, but step() applies no containment, so within about one second of play the graph is 8-20 units across with 0.06 m nodes - a hairline cobweb sprawling far outside its map cell. Two of the four placements (Test_Substrates, Zone_TemporalStorage) stand in ordinary rooms. That is a defect to decide about, not an axis to declare, and capping it would change what all 4 placements look like.",
    "also": "The layout is additionally unseeded (Grid3DCartridge.initialize uses global randf/randf_range) and time-domain (get_warmup_steps() is 0, so the still is whatever 1.1 s of relaxation reached). Both are fixable with a seed export and a warmup fixture; neither is the blocker. force_directed_layout in algorithms_misc.json is a DIFFERENT script (algorithms/graphtheory/force_directed_layout/) and shares nothing with this one - its earlier refusal is a separate question. grid3d_substrate.tscn is shared by nine tokens (grid3d, _bfs, _dfs, _dijkstra, _kruskal, _prim, _force_directed, _random_graph, _entropy), which pick their cartridge from the artifact_lookup_name meta."
   },
